    <name>
      <text>Simple interest: time given in months (INNODEMS)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>{@nm@} invests Ksh \( {@P0@} \) in a \( {@m0@} \)-month fixed deposit account that earns simple interest at \( {@rd(R0)@}\% \) per annum.</p>
<p>(a) Write the time in years, as a fraction or decimal.</p>
<div>\( T = \) [[input:ans1]] years [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p>(b) Calculate the interest earned at the end of the \( {@m0@} \) months.</p>
<div>Interest \( = \) Ksh [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>(a)</strong> The rate is <em>per annum</em> (per year), so the time must be in years: \( T = \dfrac{ {@m0@} }{12} = {@rd(T0)@} \) years.</p>
<p><strong>(b)</strong></p>
\[ I = \frac{P \times R \times T}{100} = \frac{ {@P0@} \times {@rd(R0)@} \times {@m0@} }{100 \times 12} = {@r2(si)@}. \]
<p>The interest earned is Ksh \( {@r2(si)@} \).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
